spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed], bg black
  foreground:
    color: single non-green, non-black color
    shape: irregular blob placed on the grid with bbox 4-6 rows x 4-7 cols
    bbox_fill_ratio: 0.4-0.8; fg pixels have holes/gaps within each half
    margins: bbox offset >=1 from every grid edge
  separator:
    exactly one full-grid row or column (all-black in input) that lies strictly inside the fg bbox
    splits fg into two non-empty halves (fg pixels on both sides)
    no other all-bg row or column exists strictly inside the bbox
  output:
    paint the separator row/column green across the entire grid; all other pixels unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Choose grid 10x10, pick fg_color from {1,2,4,5,6,7,8,9} (not green=3)
    2. Pick separator axis (row or col) and index ensuring >=1 margin on all sides of final bbox
    3. Build two independent fg half-regions on opposite sides of the separator
       - each half spans 1-4 rows (or cols) and 2-6 cols (or rows)
       - place random fg pixels in each half (fill 40-80% of half bbox area)
       - ensure at least one fg pixel on each boundary row/col of overall bbox
    4. Verify exactly one all-bg row/col strictly inside the combined fg bbox (the separator)
       and no accidental other all-bg row/col inside bbox; if violated, add fg pixels to fix
    5. Output = input with separator row/col painted green across full grid width/height
```
