0012: 
0013: def main(input_grid):
0014:     """
0015:     Trace a bouncing blue diagonal path upward and recolor the black background teal.
0016: 
0017:     Input structure:
0018:     - The grid has a black background with exactly one blue pixel.
0019:     - The blue pixel is the start of an upward-right diagonal ray.
0020:     - The left and right grid edges act as reflection walls.
0021: 
0022:     Rule:
0023:     - Starting from the blue pixel, draw blue one step up and horizontally each move.
0024:     - Reverse horizontal direction when the next step would leave the grid.
0025:     - Stop when the path exits through the top, then change remaining black cells to teal.
0026: 
0027:     Key insight:
0028:     - The path behaves like a diagonal ray reflecting only off vertical walls before the
0029:       final background recoloring.
0030:     """
0031:     # Plan:
0032:     # 1. Detect the pixel
0033:     # 2. Shoot each line of the reflection one-by-one, bouncing (changing horizontal direction) when it hits a (horizontal) wall/edge of canvas
0034:     # 3. Change the background color to teal
0035: 
0036:     # Locate the blue pixel.
0037:     coords = np.argwhere(input_grid == Color.BLUE)
